What the public copy serves. Copies, made by hand:
  tour.json   <- bun gen/materialize.ts --repo /bulk3/runs/readback/kuitti-live --plan data/kuitti-3-full/plan.json --out data/live/tour.json --rest
                 (full read, PR head 55559f7, 11 planted lines; --rest adds the last stop with the 282 changed lines no other stop shows)
  short.json  <- data/kuitti-3-short/tour.json  (short read: 2 stops, with the cold test)
The short read is made by:
  bun gen/short.ts --plan data/kuitti-3-full/plan.json --stops share-token,searched-list --cold "src/lib/invoices.ts:50-87" --cold-plants plant-invoices-61 --no-plants plant-invoices-147 --out data/kuitti-3-short/plan.json
  bun gen/materialize.ts --repo /bulk3/runs/readback/kuitti-live --plan data/kuitti-3-short/plan.json

evidence.json  <- data/kuitti-3-full/evidence.json (the Evidence interface in shared/tour.ts), made by:
  bun gen/evidence.ts --repo /bulk3/runs/readback/kuitti-live --plan data/kuitti-3-full/plan.json --out data/kuitti-3-full --copy data/live --earlier /bulk3/runs/readback/kuitti-2-head-55559f7/steps --resume
What is in it and where it comes from:
  tests      one run of `bun test` on head 55559f7, in Docker (oven/bun:1), no network
  changes    one-line changes, each run alone against all tests the same way. claude-opus-5-5 proposes about 7 per stop
             in a copy of the head commit without the test files; the 11 planted lines of plan.json and the candidates
             of the earlier plant steps (--earlier) are tried too. A change whose run broke without a failing test,
             timed out, or failed more than 40% of the tests (the app no longer starts) is not counted.
             claude-fable-5-2 then checks every change the tests did not notice and drops the ones that do the same
             as the original line.
  criteria, risk   claude-fable-5-2 reads the stops and the issue; code checks that the code quoted in riskWhy is in the stop
  route      decided in code from the fields above, no model
  rulings    claude-fable-5-2 proposes; code checks every cited range, and that an "untested" item cites a line
             where a change went unnoticed by the tests
Model answers, every test run, all tried changes (changes.json) and the step log (evidence.log.jsonl) are kept in
/bulk3/runs/readback/evidence/kuitti-3-full-55559f7/ (no backups). --resume reuses them, so a rerun asks no model again.

questions.json  <- bun gen/questions.ts (see its header): a pool of questions per stop, written by one model and checked by a
                   second one twice, with the stop's code and without it. A question the checker gets right without the code
                   is dropped. Each reviewer is asked a draw of the pool (server/app.ts drawOf).
entire.json     <- bun gen/entire.ts --repo /bulk3/runs/readback/entire/kuitti --tour data/live/tour.json --out data/live --findings /bulk3/runs/readback/entire/findings.json
                   the agent sessions behind the lines (entire blame, checkpoints), what calls each changed function (entire graph), the trail
efficiency.json <- bun gen/efficiency.ts --entire data/live/entire.json --head <checkout of 55559f7> --out /bulk3/runs/readback/efficiency/out
                   "what calls this function?" asked of Entire's graph and of claude-opus-5-5 with read tools, for all 37 changed functions
